{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/842531-moving-down-the-tiers-conspiracies-into-compacts","id":842531,"title":"Moving Down the Tiers: Conspiracies into Compacts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-03-05T06:52:52-08:00","id":842531,"title":"Moving Down the Tiers: Conspiracies into Compacts","content":"Over in the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/398609-moving-up-the-tiers-2\">Moving Up the Tiers</a> thread, I said that if nothing else, it was a way to rearrange which hunter groups got odd powers and which didn't. But what about the other way? Less sexy, sure, but what would make good 1-dot status benefits and compact-style Endowments for the existing conspiracies? Ones that remove - or severely reduce - their supernatural capability, while retaining their basic feel?<br /> <br /> Aegis kai Doru: This would logically be a group that locks relics away or destroys them rather than using them, figuring the risk of them falling into enemy hands outweighs their usefulness. I can't think of an Endowment unless that oath of theirs gives them some oomph. But people with a talent for ancient bling can probably get valuable shit as well as mystical: at Status 1, they get a free dot of Resources for use in the Vigil.<br /> <br /> Ascending Ones: As I've observed in the past, this is more an alliance of three groups than one. As such, I propose a different Status 1 benefit for each one; ironically, on checking, two are the same as the rules in Compacts and Conspiracies: Academics (religion) for the religious faction and Streetwise (territories) for the gang side. The alchemists should get Science (pharmacology) - while this might seem dissonant, the Ascending Ones as a <i>compact</i> is assuming they discovered some relevant science &quot;early&quot; rather than discovering anything supernatural. For the Endowment... they have a drug: maybe it eliminates wound penalties for a scene, maybe it adds +3 to resist mind altering powers also for a scene, something like that. The Endowment is Doses: that's how many doses the hunter has on hand (it refills between stories, or when there's a suitable pause that would provide an opportunity). Since they're physical objects, hunters can give each other their doses of the drug mid-story (the dots don't move of course); Safe Houses can also be invested with additional Doses.<br /> <br /> Cainite Heresy: What could their Status 1 benefit be but an Occult specialty in vampires? Their Endowment is Fanatical Hatred: dots are added to their rolls to resist the mental powers of vampires (or other monsters they credibly believe are vampires). They also won't surrender to powers like the Kiss.<br /> <br /> Cheiron Group: The Cheiron Group can have the same purpose and way of hunting without having figured out how to implant bits of monster into its operatives. In which case, I would guess an appropriate Endowment would be Requisitions, as below for TFV. The corporation knows what its asking of their people, and is generous in kitting them out.<br /> <br /> Faithful of Shulpae: An iron stomach - seriously - immune to anything that's not actively poisonous. Endowment... Empowerment. Having taken in the essence of the gods, so they think, the Faithful enjoy a bolstered confidence. Dots in Empowerment are akin to Willpower - they provide only +1 rather than +3, but act on every roll for a single scene.<br /> <br /> Knights of St Adrian: ??<br /> <br /> Knights of St George: ??<br /> <br /> Les Mysteres: They do learn to understand spirits, even if they don't have specific magic for dealing with them. An Occult specialty in spirits at Status 1. Endowment... maybe psychological training to put themselves in the right mindset for the resonance a particular spirit needs to manifest?<br /> <br /> Lucifuge: Occult specialty in demons at Status 1. Endowment... they get an Unseen Sense for demons for free, and can use it to pinpoint a demon or demoniac once per dot per session before having to resort to the spooked condition ... or maybe Fame, but applied to demons, those who know the character and her parentage tending to resentfully back off.<br /> <br /> Malleus Maleficarum: A (religion) specialty in Expression, Persuasion, or Socialise - though I'm not sure whether the hunter should get to pick one, or the list get narrowed down - but they know the right things to say to convince their co-religionists of things they might not otherwise accept. Endowment... Consecrated Items: blessed objects that can be used in exorcisms, abjurations, and wardings; each dot represents one item that can be subbed for a specific ban or bane. However many items a member has, he must use all of them to get any benefit.<br /> Task Force VALKYRIE: The Untouchable Merit at Status 1, for crimes committed in service to the mission (representing cover from superiors rather than your own efforts). Endowment... maybe Requisitions, where you have a floating set of Resource dots to secure high tech (but not supertech) equipment.<br /> <br /> VASCU: A logical Endowment would be Files: access to law enforcement databases and case files, counting as an equipment bonus to forensic and profiling rolls (well, all VASCU people will have that with the time; the Endowment would be the shit you've memorised).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":321,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","user":"SunlessNick","date":". 03-07-2016, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-05T11:33:56-08:00","id":842660,"title":"","content":"I don't have time to give an extensive look to your suggestion- but I'll keep following this thread. color me interested","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-07T06:48:21-08:00","id":843395,"title":"","content":"Added ideas for the Ascending Ones, Malleus Maleficarum, Faithful of Shulpae, Cainite Heresy, and Cheiron Group.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/321-sunlessnick","name":"SunlessNick","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1214"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T02:16:49-07:00","id":846981,"title":"","content":"In mirrors, it allows for people to alter the local resonance, basically using feng shui, akin to that merit from werewolf second edition, so I suggest making the resonance alteration a bit more active.<br /> <br /> Have you considered using the crafting rules from chronicles of darkness? I could easily see several hunter factions getting specialties in crafting supernatural enhancements of the appropriate flavor- An AO would enjoy a specialty in making a potion of swimming, an inquisitor might be able to bless a weapon to make it strike true, an aegis member might be able to make &quot;good luck charms,&quot; etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/391-stsword","name":"StSword","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar391_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1635"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-03-14T09:38:02-07:00","id":847138,"title":"","content":"I must say I imagine the compact version of Cheiron Group operates as Nebula from Durarara- that is, some sort of local pharmaceutical company which experiments on both humans and supernatural beings in order to discover all kinds of new development for their business.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/